SECTION 4 — GLOBAL AUTHORITY MODEL AND STRICT SEPARATION OF RESPONSIBILITIES
===============================================================================

4.1 WHY AUTHORITY MUST BE EXPLICIT

The system contains several mechanisms capable of appearing authoritative:

- systemd;
- deterministic supervisor;
- Meta Luna;
- Luna sub-orchestrators;
- Hermes gateway dispatcher;
- native Hermes Kanban;
- Hermes Studio UI;
- Conductor;
- Crews;
- Git;
- project database;
- requirements ledger;
- review records;
- release gate.

If authority is ambiguous, agents will create duplicated state machines.

That causes:

- duplicate workers;
- conflicting status;
- phantom completion;
- stale UI;
- races;
- lost recovery.

Therefore each authority receives a narrow contract.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.2 DETERMINISTIC SUPERVISOR AUTHORITY

The deterministic supervisor owns:

    LIVENESS

It may:

- monitor heartbeat;
- track process IDs;
- detect stale directors/managers;
- hold retry counters;
- select a configured recovery action;
- relaunch Meta Luna;
- emit recovery directives;
- observe completion-gate result;
- maintain pause/resume flags.

It may NOT:

- interpret product requirements;
- create implementation tasks directly unless explicitly instructed by Meta
  Luna through a narrow deterministic interface;
- claim Kanban work;
- decide architecture;
- approve implementation;
- merge code;
- mark SHIPPED.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.3 META-LUNA AUTHORITY

Meta Luna owns:

    PROGRAM COHERENCE

Meta Luna determines:

- what workstream should run;
- dependency ordering;
- which Luna manager receives a workstream;
- which strong model should review/challenge;
- whether evidence is sufficient to advance a phase;
- whether architecture needs reopening;
- when to invoke release gates.

Meta Luna does not own:

- implementation code authorship;
- independent QA approval;
- final SHIPPED authority.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.4 LUNA SUB-ORCHESTRATOR AUTHORITY

A Luna sub-orchestrator owns:

    BOUNDED WORKSTREAM MANAGEMENT

It may:

- inspect;
- plan within frozen contracts;
- create implementation cards;
- monitor child workers;
- run deterministic checks;
- request reviews;
- issue rework.

It may not:

- redefine global architecture unilaterally;
- write implementation code;
- self-review;
- declare project release.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.5 HERMES KANBAN AUTHORITY

The verified native durable Hermes Kanban or actual equivalent owns:

    BUILD TASK LIFECYCLE

It should represent:

- implementation task queue;
- assignment;
- dependency;
- active execution;
- review state where supported;
